A||||8||Dan86gt3.8||HELP!- has anyone ever had their radaitor fan go south?||||8||
Z||000000||Dan86gt3.8||08-23-2000||07:38 PM||||Ok 1st thins first i go off to school with a brand new yellow paint job feeling great about my car.  and the first thing that I see when I come out into the parking lot of my apartment is the damn exhaust hanger broke on the right side and my right side tip isabut 5 inches lower than it usually is.  So sinse I am away from home and my dads wonderfull huge tool box I had to go get a frigin coat hanger and do the famous wire the exaust up in place trick.<P>Anywho to get to the point today I was driving around and it was hot as hell (in the high 90's-low 100's) we had just got out of a little shop and got in and was sitting at a light, I glanced down at the temp and it was pegged I quickly pulled over into a jack in the crack and waited for it too cool down.  I got it back to the apartment and was trying to figure out what in the hell was wrong.  Then I realized that the ignition was on but the fan was not on.  Correct me if I am wrong but I thought anytimne the igniton was on that the fan should be running.  Because everytim in the past I turned the igniton on the fan kicked up.   Anywho is this a common thing like the headlight motors?  Is it most likely the fan or is thier realys that go out or what?  I am about to call and get the advice from dear old dad.  But would greatly appreciate input from you guys.  Also how much is the part AND WOULD IT BE A GOOD IDEA TO GET A NEW ONE.  also do you have to take off the hood to get tha damn thing out or is it relitively easy to get out?  W ell sorry for the longevity of the post but I had to rant!<P>ps- if you go to college try and take your parents garage with you!<P>------------------<BR>86 gt fiero<BR>3.8/4speed auto<BR>ace conversion kit<BR>15" konig monsoon's<BR>rear swaybar/ and urethane on rear.<BR>Soon to come urethane all the way around. and new yellow paint w/ raised spoiler!!!!<BR>(also in way future years forced induction on my 3.8!!!!!!!!!)||||reg||8
Z||000001||terryk||08-23-2000||09:35 PM||||Yes, mine died. Solder joint in the relay broke. Motors go bad too.<P>Fan is only on when the switch in the engine closed or the AC is on.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 08-23-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mattsfiero||08-23-2000||10:34 PM||||Okay my fan does something simialar when I turn on the ignition it turns on but if I let the car Idle too long the fan will turn off and the car overheats....Haven't figured it out yet...let me know what you find out.<P>Matt||||reg||1
Z||000003||DaveL||08-24-2000||08:55 AM||||Someone has probably rewired the fan to run all the time, a good thing if you ask me. They are supposed to run whenever the a/c is on ayway, which is most of the time if you live anywhere halfway hot. <BR>Use a voltage tester to see if you have voltage at the fan connector, meaning the plug on the fan, with your ignition on. If there is voltage, then the fan just burnt out. They are super easy to replace, and only cost $20-$30. If not, you may have a relay or temp sensor problem, which is out of my league. Mine is wired to run whenever the switch is on. Occasionally gets a little warmer than usual if sitting at too many red lights, but never near overheating.<BR>They can be replaced without removing the hood, but you will have to open it. When I was replacing my fan, I accidentally knocked into the arm that holds the hood up and it fell on me. I could see the headline now, "Local Man eaten by Fiero".....||||reg||1
Z||000004||My7Fieros||08-24-2000||10:40 PM||||The fan dosnt come on until the engine reaches around 235 degrees (just past the halfway mark on the guage for 6 bangers), or when the a/c is turned on...it dosnt run all the time.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Rodney||08-25-2000||01:04 PM||||You can run a lower temp thermostat and a lower temp fan switch. I have both on my web page. I have just recieved a batch of fan switches I had made for me by the same manufacturer that supplies fan switches to Echlin. Echlin is top quality stuff. My price is lower now also now. $24.00 for the fan switch. These are 185-195 switches. Turns on at 195 and shuts off at 185. That and the 180 degree Stant thermostat and your engine will stay nice and cool. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||WKDFIRO||08-25-2000||02:48 PM||||If you turn on the AC and the fan is running then everything is pretty much okay from there. (84s being the only possible exception with its multi speed fans and relays.) If you are not sure about the fan motor you can swap it out with the fan motor that is used in your AC and vents. They are the same motor. This way you have a proven part to test the system and is Plan B (85 - 88 ony) if you are out in the middle of no where with a bad fan motor.<P>On my Fiero I have a manual override switch to simply turn on the fan and engine blowers (on the same circuit) when ever I want to. Ridiculously easy if you know what you are doing.<P>Hope this helps.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Dan86gt3.8||08-25-2000||05:43 PM||||Ok today my dad brought me an old fan and some tools.  We swapped the fan then he took off and went home.  Well i get in my car and go down to pay for classes and there was a big traffic jam so I sat around iding alott.  Well after about 10 minuts of sitting still it started getting hot.  Finally I got clear road and started cruising and got some air flowing over the radiator and it started cooling down.  On the way home though I was driving a steady speed and it I saw it getting hotter and heard the coolant overflowing.  So I parked it and let it cool down.  But on the about 1/'2 mile trip on the way home it the temp stared skyrocketing.  I got it home and got it parked.<P>Here is whaty I know/thinking.  The repklacement fan is spinnig couer clockwise, I thought the old one used to spin clockwise. I can also hear it rubbing something, but can't se it rub anything.  Second is yall have mntioned ac, I have ac but the lines are not hooked up and the system is not charged.  I am thinking thier might be some air in the coolant system.  I think I can check that by parking on one of the many very steep hills around town here and see if the radiator will take any water.  Also the fan might be running constantly because of something ACE did in the wiring harness to make the fan run constantly.  <BR>So right now all I can thin of is checking for air in the system.....<BR>thanks for the input guys!<BR><P>------------------<BR>86 gt fiero<BR>3.8/4speed auto<BR>ace conversion kit<BR>15" konig monsoon's<BR>rear swaybar/ and urethane on rear.<BR>Soon to come urethane all the way around. and new yellow paint w/ raised spoiler!!!!<BR>(also in way future years forced induction on my 3.8!!!!!!!!!)||||reg||5
Z||000008||Phil||08-25-2000||07:11 PM||||ACE did my conversion and my fan does not run constantly, just when needed.||||reg||1
